   "created_at": "2026-11-08T20:58:57Z",
   "updated_at": "2026-11-08T20:58:57Z",
   "body": "Fixed on [fix/5628-reset-history-preservation](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/5628-reset-history-preservation), commit [dcaea432](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/dcaea43244615808b3ff284303e71d12f9191166), based on upstream `ed0ab567`.\n\n`noteResetUsed` now distinguishes a missing record from a read failure. A read failure is returned without replacing the file; malformed JSON is replaced only after its exact bytes have been successfully saved aside. A failed backup is returned and leaves the original intact. The existing caller still reports a local recording error without treating the already-spent reset as unspent.\n\nOn Linux as a non-root user, permission fixtures demonstrate the original read and backup failures and pass with the fix, checking original bytes and the underlying permission error. Existing missing/valid/corrupt-record cases and the public reset caller test pass with `-race`; provider vet/build pass. I independently reran the focused race tests. Windows was cross-compiled only; no full suite or real reset service was run. AI-assisted implementation and review.",
